course: dictionary
lesson: 14559
title: Photographic: pictures in words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from parts you may already know. Photographic comes from photograph, a picture made by a camera, and the ending -ic often means to do with. So photographic means to do with photographs or photography. «The photographic studio had bright lights and a big white backdrop.» A studio where people have photos taken is to do with photography, so the clue fits the meaning.
explain: Look at the words around it to check. «The police found photographic evidence of the crime: clear pictures taken by a camera.» The words evidence and clear pictures tell you that photographic means made from photos.
explain: Photographic also has a second meaning. «Mia has a photographic memory, so she remembers every page she has read.» Here it has nothing to do with a camera. It means remembering things in great detail, as if they were a picture in your mind. Ask yourself: does the sentence fit a camera, or a memory? The clues decide.
fact: Photographic means to do with photographs or photography.
fact: «Photographic» comes from «photograph», and the ending «-ic» often means to do with.
fact: «Photographic evidence» means pictures taken by a camera that show what happened.
fact: A «photographic memory» lets someone remember things in great detail, like a picture.
fact: True photographic memory is very rare, and some scientists think it may not exist at all.
exercise: «The photographic studio had bright lights and a big white backdrop.» What does photographic mean here? | *To do with photographs or photography | Very old and dusty | To do with swimming pools | Loud and noisy
exercise: «Mia has a photographic memory, so she remembers every page she has read.» What does a photographic memory let Mia do? | Take photos with her mind | *Remember things in great detail, like a picture | Read very slowly | Forget things quickly
exercise: «The police found photographic evidence of the crime.» What kind of evidence is it? | Footprints in the mud | Words written in a diary | Sounds recorded by a microphone | *Pictures taken by a camera
test: «The camera shop sells photographic film for old cameras.» What is photographic film? | A kind of sweet | *Film used for taking photos | Film about cats and dogs | A thin layer of ice on a pond
test: Ruby says, «I have a photographic memory, so I never forget a face.» What does Ruby mean? | She cannot see very well | She takes lots of photos on her phone | *She remembers faces in great detail, like a picture | She forgets things easily
exam: Why might a teacher say that a true photographic memory is rare? | *Because it is very rare and may not exist at all | Because everyone has one, so it is easy to find | Because it is a kind of camera | Because it means taking photos with your phone
